  "checks": [
    "Existing composer and execution settings receive only current-provider models; the root shared catalog remains complete. One shared helper handles scoped rows and explicit aliases; unlabelled rows are admitted only in a complete entirely legacy directory.",
    "Partial catalogs cannot disprove aliases. Unknown selections preserve drafts and block uncertain sends; only proven foreign model/provider/effort overrides are removed, retaining text, attachments and unrelated settings.",
    "Conversion is an explicit top-right menu. Two intentional steps bind source/epoch and target model/effort. Repeated click/key press cannot skip confirmation; only thread/convert is submitted, never user input.",
    "Late responses are scoped; known new identity goes through draft-safe workflow handoff. Pending/unknown operations block conflicting auto-resume; receipt reconciliation queries the same operation without resubmission. Accepted conversion is consumed only by the destination history load.",
    "Sidebars refresh on accepted and uncertain conversion receipts, including other tabs. Existing project/thread lifecycle refresh and all-provider thread listing remain intact.",
    "README/FEATURES/architecture/recovery/verification describe new independent copy semantics, ordinary compacted history support and unsupported encrypted/inherited history honestly. Original provider must remain available; returning to original does not undo shared workspace/external changes.",
    "Old inline conversion confirmation and repair routes/components/tests/styles were removed; no remaining active callers. Current API/operations changes were independently reviewed by other partition reviewers."
  ],
